WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.850
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:11.960
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.530
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:26.300
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:34.050
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.520
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.390
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:44.120
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.790
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.470
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.470 --> 00:01:01.140
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.510
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:12.150
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:17.060
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.300
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:32.410
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:37.140
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.880
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.040
Little Narumi?!

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:54.920
What do you want,
Mr. Dripping-Wet Loser?

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.460
Even losers have pride.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.590
Let's make a trade.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.700
"All That You Can Do"

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.150
<i>We have complete hold
over Hiyono-san's life.</i>

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.590
Do you really think we
can make an equal trade?

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.090
If she's killed,

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.960
then I won't hesitate to
submit the tape to the police.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.530
You probably have escape preparations too,

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.970
but your actions this time
are remarkably limited.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.600
Plus you're still seriously ill.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.810
You'd prefer to avoid police
intervention if possible, right?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.240
So that's why you can't
kill her right now.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.150
But conversely,

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.120
as long as she's alive, I can't
ask for police assistance.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.990
The instant I do, you'll kill her.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:01.820
Because there's no point
in keeping her alive

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.620
if that tape winds up in police hands.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.290
We're each holding the other's weakness,

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:10.000
but as a result, neither
of us can make a move.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.230
Even if a thousand days
passed, this wouldn't change.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:16.070
So you want to trade
the girl for the tape?

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.640
As if we'd ever agree to such a deal.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.740
You could make dozens
of copies of the tape.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.940
No, I won't make any copies.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.210
Your word doesn't amount to crap.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:32.550
Look, even if I safely rescued her

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:36.260
there's the possibility of being
targeted later for revenge...

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.420
I need to ensure her safety,
even long into the future.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.790
That's what this trade is for.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.640
There's more than one way
to put it, Little Narumi.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.940
If you don't hand over the tape

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.340
<i>we can get rid of Hiyono-san
at any time, you know.</i>

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.720
My only choice is to immediately
hand it over if you do,

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.210
but you won't.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.260
You're not the kind of
people who would be satisfied

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.260
if I surrendered because of such violence.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.830
I'm not proposing a simple deal or exchange.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.800
I'm proposing we finish
what we started yesterday.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.700
You want to exterminate me, don't you?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.730
You'll let us?

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:33.770
The lightning, pika pika pika ri

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.750
<i>Come on, Narumi-san!</i>

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.350
If you don't save her soon,

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:41.080
the imprisoned princess
will escape on her own!

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:44.690
Let me tell you one thing in advance.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.490
"If we exercise angel-like fairness

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.360
and give Little Narumi a chance to fight

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.030
<i>and a chance for victory,</i>

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.870
then we're also prepared
to snatch his life away

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.230
like a demon."

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.010
<i>That was a restriction we
and Kiyotaka-sama agreed to.</i>

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:04.640
<i>In other words, I can exterminate
you in this situation.</i>

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.780
So if you give your
opponent the same chance,

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:08.870
then being unfair and
deceitful is fine, huh?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.690
<i>That explains why you do
everything like a game.</i>

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.310
<i>Little Narumi...</i>

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.990
<i>If you can make a comeback now,</i>

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.520
<i>then it's just as Kiyotaka said...</i>

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.900
Exactly what kind of trade
is it you wanna make?

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.070
We each have something the other wants.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.740
The tape and the hostage...

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:39.150
Whoever obtains both is the victor, yes?

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.250
Of course.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.850
So here's my suggestion.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:45.150
Right now, the tape is in a
place where I can't recover it

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.420
until after 2:00 pm tomorrow.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:51.620
And I set things up so that
it'll wind up in police hands

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.560
if by some chance something
should happen to me.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.700
In other words,

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.100
you guys can't carelessly injure me,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.770
but on the other hand, if
you learn the hiding place

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:04.500
and can arrive there before
I do, you can steal the tape.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:05.570
Continue.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:08.540
You just give me the same chance.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:13.780
At 1:30 pm tomorrow, I'll tell
you where the tape is hidden.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:14.380
At the same time...

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:19.590
At the same time, we tell you
where the girl is confined.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.720
<i>So it is a simple exchange.</i>

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.220
No.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.390
We know each other's destinations.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:29.830
Don't you think you could
hinder your opponent?

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:30.730
In other words,

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:34.570
you're trying to say it's possible
to obtain both given the chance?

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:35.870
Exactly.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.540
That's the kind of game I'm proposing.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:39.670
The one who gets both treasures

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:44.280
while blocking their opponent wins...

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.850
The rules are a bit vague.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:49.020
You can decide on those.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.350
Try to make it a fair game of wits.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.440
<i>That is my trade.</i>

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.560
Will you accept this match?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.920
Or will you run away?

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.370
Fine.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.530
But I'm sure you'll regret
acting so tough now!

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:16.300
Just try and make me.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:22.880
We've been had!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.940
<i>Hiyono-san was right!</i>

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:29.590
That wasn't the same Little
Narumi as before!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.060
What do you mean?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.730
The Little Narumi up until
now never liked himself

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.560
so he never had any confidence,

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.070
and his purpose for fighting
was ambiguous and weak.

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:44.900
<i>But now he has a very clear
purpose: Rescuing Hiyono-san!</i>

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:51.010
<i>Being a hostage would make
Narumi-san more spirited!</i>

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.540
That girl has turned
everything upside-down!

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:00.820
Idiot!

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.860
You can still win, you know.

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.360
And it's not like you to
be scared that easily.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:08.130
Yeah, you're right. Sorry.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.030
Let's start figuring out a way

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:13.700
to outwit and bring death
upon that Little Narumi.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:14.700
Yeah.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.770
Alright!

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:18.860
Even if you do have pride,
I'll make you regret it!

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:25.040
<i>Looks like I managed to drag
that girl into the game...</i>

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.240
<i>Now the real show starts.</i>

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.630
We're playing a happy little game.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.560
Another game?

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:43.730
We weren't the ones who suggested it.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.530
This time it was Little Narumi.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.470
Really?!

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:49.960
I can't wait!

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:02.080
Praying to God?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.850
There's no such thing as God.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.520
Is it okay for you to walk around?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.260
No. I need two more weeks of rest.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:13.350
But this is no time for
me to be lying in bed.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.730
Well then, allow me to explain the game.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.850
The object of the game is to
get both the tape and the girl,

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:37.250
which will be located in
different parts of town.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.350
There are obstacles, naturally.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.590
No complicated rules.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:44.720
I'm giving this to you.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.830
What's this key for?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:53.730
It disarms a bomb that's been
set in a certain location.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:59.040
Naturally, if you can't disarm
it within the time limit...kaboom.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:01.640
Where is this certain location?

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:03.470
Wouldn't you like to know...

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.250
Little Narumi's neck.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.740
It's small, but powerful
enough to blow your head off.

00:10:14.450 --> 00:10:17.790
The bomb will explode at 2:30 by my watch.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:21.330
Please synchronize your watch with mine.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.330
This goes without saying, of course,

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:27.000
but the collar won't come
off unless you use the key.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.670
If you try to forcibly remove it...

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.070
Kaboom, right?

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.840
<i>The key has been given to Hiyono-san.</i>

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.270
Your time limit is one hour -

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:37.470
if you can meet her before
then, you'll survive.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.480
But if you do anything in
the middle of the game

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.680
like get the police involved
or ask other people for help

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.950
the collar will explode immediately.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.420
You'd do it too, huh?

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:52.630
Now then, at 1:30 the game will start

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.060
<i>and Hiyono-san will be released.</i>

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:58.800
How you decide to use her is up to you.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.970
So you want a fair 2-on-2 match, huh?

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.840
I suppose you could say that.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:08.910
But we won't touch her for the first
10 minutes after the game starts.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.980
After that, we'll start
making moves to capture her.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.980
Also, if we get the tape first,

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.390
<i>we'll eliminate Hiyono-san
without hesitation.</i>

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:22.190
We're allowed to obstruct our
opponents from achieving their goal,

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:23.490
so that's only natural...

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.490
<i>Hiyono-san has a cell phone, as do we.</i>

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.530
You can ask her for her
present location yourself.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:34.200
All four of our numbers are programmed in,

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.670
so you can also call your opponents.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.770
And it's also up to you to
accept an opponent's call or not.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.010
That's thoughtful of you.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:44.410
<i>This is a large battle field.</i>

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:48.310
There'd be no way to coordinate
strategies without the phones.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.620
<i>Think...</i>

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:53.550
<i>If I try to meet her while
on my way to get the tape,</i>

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:56.760
<i>it would have to be at
a place near the tape.</i>

00:11:56.760 --> 00:12:00.390
<i>Naturally, these guys would
be homing in on that location,</i>

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.330
<i>which would increase the
risk of her being attacked.</i>

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.370
<i>But if I make our meeting
point a distant location</i>

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.900
<i>the chance of the tape falling
into enemy hands is high.</i>

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:14.510
<i>But if I elude the enemy and try
to meet her after getting the tape,</i>

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.840
<i>there might not be enough time...</i>

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:21.170
<i>I'm walking a tightrope,
no matter what I do...</i>

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:25.050
Are you regretting it now?

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.720
Sorry to be so sudden,

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.720
but do you mind if I
confirm that she's well?

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:30.750
Be my guest.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.230
<i>Narumi-san?!</i>

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:40.730
Yo. I'm gonna save you, stupid girl.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.830
<i>Bye.</i>

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.900
Eh? Wait...

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.740
Is that all?! The nerve of him!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.810
"Are you all right, my fair princess?"

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.010
"They're not treating you badly, are they?"

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.180
Couldn't he have said something like that?!

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:54.870
Don't look at me!

00:12:55.680 --> 00:13:00.350
So where is the tape?

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.620
The post office.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.890
I sealed it securely and
mailed it to myself.

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.290
It should arrive around 2:00 pm today.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.230
I see. Good thinking.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:11.130
I think you've realized by now,

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:13.700
but even if you arrive
before me to check the mail

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:16.900
you won't be able to steal the
tape if it hasn't been delivered.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.640
A mailbox key?

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:24.140
It's an apartment building.

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:27.850
Next to the manager's office there
are mailboxes for all the tenants.

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:31.050
Apparently for anti-theft purposes
and protection of privacy.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.950
If I die and you guys can't steal the tape,

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.720
my sister-in-law will check
the suspicious package.

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.160
Basically meaning the police will have it.

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.730
Impressive.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:46.430
You've really thought of everything.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.200
Couldn't you predict that?

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:54.040
I predicted you would put
this kind of bomb on me.

00:13:54.670 --> 00:14:00.210
<i>Now timing is more important
than being the first one there.</i>

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.850
<i>Kosuke-kun is near Little Narumi's house,</i>

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.680
<i>but now there's no point
in having him rush there.</i>

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.690
<i>This key is a bottleneck.</i>

00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:09.790
<i>We don't need it to open the mailbox,</i>

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:14.090
<i>but we run the risk of being
seen by residents or the manager.</i>

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:18.230
<i>Which means now I have to make a move.</i>

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.060
<i>This is going to cost us a lot.</i>

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:26.970
Good. The stage is now set.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.960
The time limit is one hour.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:42.040
Let the game begin.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.720
If you don't want Little Narumi to die,

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.460
then you'll run like the wind.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:50.220
I won't let you catch me twice!

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:56.090
Ten minutes...That's a
pretty long head start...

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:03.410
Rio. I just released the girl.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:06.150
Then I'll explain our strategy.

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:10.220
<i>Narumi-san, the weather now makes
it seem like that storm wasn't real!</i>

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.620
Yeah. Where are you now?

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:13.750
On an embankment.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.690
I see a river to my right and
a railroad bridge up ahead,

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:20.030
so I'm about a quarter mile
south of Shumari Station!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:21.590
I'm near the church.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:23.200
Over a mile and a half away.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:25.360
<i>Narumi-san! Just let them get the tape;</i>

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.770
let's remove the bomb
around your neck first!

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.140
There's nothing to be gained if you die!

00:15:30.140 --> 00:15:31.500
No.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.970
There's no point to this match
unless it's a complete victory!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:36.640
So the tape comes first.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:39.080
You sure are assertive

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.210
when someone's really worried about you!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.050
I want this thing off as
quickly as possible too,

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:45.720
but I can't, thanks to you.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:46.490
Come again?

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:48.320
You went too far.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:51.360
They're ready to get rid of you, you know.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:53.560
If they get the tape, they'll
eliminate you immediately,

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.330
regardless of the game.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.330
Worry more about yourself.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:59.260
Listen, the tape comes first.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:00.500
I'm going to sweat bullets,

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.530
but the bomb key will have
to wait until the very end.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.470
What should I do?

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.470
It's all over if you're caught.

00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.510
Keep away from them until I get the tape.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:12.580
If you're near Shumari Station,
then head there and get on a train.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.210
A train?

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:17.450
You'll be safest while on a moving train.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.550
Plus they can't do anything violent
with all the passengers around.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:22.790
There's no worry of being
confined right away,

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.590
and you have a chance to
shake them off, too. Right?

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:25.690
Yeah...

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:28.690
Keep going back and forth
between the appropriate stops

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:32.200
and return to Shumari Station around 2:10.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:35.500
I'll get the bomb key from you
in the remaining 20 minutes.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.100
2:10. Got it!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:40.410
And choose the train wisely.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.710
Get on the wrong one

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.540
and you won't be able to make it
back in time before the explosion.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:48.250
<i>Got it! I will make it back in time!</i>

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.020
I'll give you my next
instructions when I get the tape.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.650
Watch yourself until then.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:53.450
I will!

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:58.120
I can tell what he's
thinking for the most part.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:58.990
Listen.

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.330
He'll put himself at risk and wait
until the last half to get the key.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.360
Getting the tape will be his priority.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.000
Yeah.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.000
<i>You rush straight for the tape, Kosuke-kun.</i>

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.200
Roger that.

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.170
What do I do about the mailbox key?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:15.540
It's a pin-cylinder lock,
so you can pick it, right?

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:19.280
I can, but it'll take 20 seconds.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.480
I'd be in messy situation
if a resident saw me.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:22.680
Just do something!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.680
There's no time to get you the key!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.150
<i>During this time,</i>

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.350
<i>I need to completely crush
Little Narumi's chances</i>

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:31.590
<i>of disarming the bomb...</i>

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:35.690
<i>There's no winning this match otherwise!</i>

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:37.930
Whatever you do, don't let your guard down.

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.200
Leave it to me!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.570
<i>First is Shumari Station...</i>

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.760
<i>I need to hurry to Shumari Station!</i>

00:17:57.080 --> 00:17:58.520
Trains out of town...

00:17:58.520 --> 00:17:59.790
Platform 1...

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:01.890
Platform 2 is for getting off only.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.220
That leaves Platforms 3 and 4.

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.930
<i>Little Narumi would think this way...</i>

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:12.760
<i>Hiyono-san needs to be in a location
where her safety will be guaranteed.</i>

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.070
<i>Which would be...</i>

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.830
<i>...inside a moving train.</i>

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.530
<i>They anticipated me!</i>

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.910
<i>Do I go outside?</i>

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:32.850
<i>No. Asazuki-san might
be ready to ambush me!</i>

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:39.090
The next train on Line 2 will
be stopping at this station.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.960
This train is out-of-service
and not boardable.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.870
The high speed express train on
Line 1, headed for Shin-Wakakusadai,

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.300
will be departing shortly.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.100
<i>High speed express?!</i>

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.070
The doors will now close.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.040
Please refrain from rushing
through the closing doors.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.840
<i>Should I get on this?</i>

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.550
Oh no!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:09.450
Bye bye!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.010
She got me!

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:14.890
Excuse me...

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:16.330
Yes?

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.930
If someone got on that
train just now by mistake,

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:24.000
around what time would they be
able to return to this station?

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.470
Just a minute...

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:31.010
It's 15 minutes until that high speed
express train makes its next stop,

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:34.810
so even if they transferred,
it would be 2:31...

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:37.450
Around 2:30.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:39.480
Thank you!

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.640
No problem...

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:44.790
<i>Time-wise, the train has
become a moving prison.</i>

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.960
<i>Now I can assume I've
destroyed any chance</i>

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.700
<i>for him to get the bomb key.</i>

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.530
<i>But even without the key,
there's still a way to survive.</i>

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.130
<i>I need to crush that, too!</i>

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.300
<i>I'm so sorry, Narumi-san!</i>

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.270
<i>Rio-san pushed me into a weird train!</i>

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:08.780
I won't make it back before the explosion!

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:09.980
Calm down!

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:12.050
It's good that you were
pushed onto the train.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:16.090
As long as you're on it you won't
be attacked during the game.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:18.090
All I have to do now is secure the tape

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:20.760
and then your safety will be secured too.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.030
I may be fine, but what about you?!

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:25.760
Now I can't give you the key!

00:20:25.760 --> 00:20:27.730
<i>Narumi-san, you're not seriously...</i>

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.200
You're not seriously thinking
that it's okay for you to die

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.860
as long as I'm saved?

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.100
<i>Answer me, Narumi-san!</i>

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:39.750
Unlike my brother, I'm a fool...

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:43.010
I have to be, or else I
can't protect anyone.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:47.390
That doesn't make me
feel any happier at all!

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:48.620
Don't worry.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.490
My death isn't guaranteed just yet.

00:20:50.490 --> 00:20:51.890
There's a way to survive.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.460
I even made the preparations...

00:20:55.460 --> 00:21:00.400
But it depends on just how
much luck and courage I have.

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:11.470
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:18.170
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:36.330
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:41.970
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:47.870
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.870 --> 00:21:54.440
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.440 --> 00:22:00.180
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:05.390
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:11.230
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:22.840
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:28.610
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:34.920
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:41.650
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:44.060 --> 00:22:47.060
One: Samurai Hiyo makes her appearance!

00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:49.160
Two: She giggles.

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:51.700
Three: She spectacularly
gets rid of the demon!

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.430
She despises the hate, not the sinner -

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.940
Samurai Hiyo plays a huge role!

00:22:55.940 --> 00:22:58.270
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:00.270
The Only Clear Option

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:03.110
The power to believe can change even fate!

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:05.480
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
